---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms and Conditions | 22 Local Marketing" description="The terms that govern the use of the 22 Local Marketing website and services.">
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-container">
      <h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: July 14, 2026</p>

      <p>These terms govern your use of this website and the services provided by 22 Local Marketing, an assumed name of Connor Dann, sole proprietor ("we", "us", "our"). By using this site or engaging our services, you agree to these terms. We keep them in plain English on purpose.</p>

      <h2>Our Services</h2>
      <p>We provide digital marketing services for home service companies, which may include website design, local SEO, Google Ads management, Google Business Profile management, and reporting. The specific scope, deliverables, and fees for your engagement are set out in a separate proposal or agreement between us. If anything in that agreement conflicts with these terms, that agreement controls.</p>

      <h2>Engagements and Billing</h2>
      <p>Our services are provided on a month-to-month basis with no long-term contract required. Fees are agreed in advance and billed on the schedule stated in your proposal. Payment is due as invoiced. Advertising budgets you set with platforms such as Google are paid to those platforms and are separate from our fees.</p>

      <h2>Client Responsibilities</h2>
      <p>To do our work, we rely on you to provide accurate business information, timely access to the accounts and assets we need, and reasonable responses to requests for approval or content. You are responsible for the accuracy of any information, photos, or claims you ask us to publish, and for making sure they are truthful and that you have the right to use them.</p>

      <h2>Ownership of Deliverables</h2>
      <p>You own the assets we build for you, including your website, domain, and marketing accounts, once fees for the related work have been paid. We may reuse general skills, methods, and non-client-specific templates in our other work.</p>

      <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>Our work depends on third-party platforms such as hosting providers, Google, and analytics and communication tools. Their availability, policies, and pricing are outside our control, and their own terms apply to your use of them.</p>

      <h2>No Guarantee of Results</h2>
      <p>We work hard to grow your leads and revenue and we report on real outcomes, but rankings, ad performance, and lead volume depend on many factors we do not control, including competition, seasonality, and platform changes. We do not guarantee specific rankings, traffic, or revenue results.</p>

      <h2>Confidentiality</h2>
      <p>We treat the business information you share with us as confidential and use it only to provide our services. See our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for how we handle personal information.</p>

      <h2>Text Messaging (SMS) Terms</h2>
      <p>If you opt in to text messages from 22 Local Marketing, here is how the program works. We send conversational messages related to your inquiry and, if you become a client, your marketing services. Examples include replies to your quote request, scheduling, and service updates. This is a customer care program, not a promotional blast list.</p>
      <p>Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply and are set by your mobile carrier, not by us. You can opt out at any time by replying STOP to any message. Reply HELP for help, or reach us at <a href="mailto:connor@22localmarketing.com">connor@22localmarketing.com</a> or (865) 348-3380. Mobile carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages. This program is intended for individuals 18 years of age or older. For details on how we handle your information, including our commitment not to share SMS opt-in data with third parties, see our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>Cancellation</h2>
      <p>Either party may end the engagement with reasonable notice as described in your proposal. Fees for work already performed remain due. On request, we will hand off the accounts and assets you own.</p>

      <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>To the extent permitted by law, our total liability for any claim relating to our services is limited to the fees you paid us for the work at issue. We are not liable for indirect or consequential losses such as lost profits.</p>

      <h2>Governing Law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of North Carolina, without regard to its conflict of law rules.</p>

      <h2>Changes to These Terms</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms from time to time. When we do, we will change the date at the top of this page. Continued use of our site or services after an update means you accept the revised terms.</p>

      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href="mailto:connor@22localmarketing.com">connor@22localmarketing.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding: 140px 24px 96px;
    background: #fff;
  }
  .legal-container {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .legal-page h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .legal-updated {
    color: #777;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .legal-page h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 36px 0 12px;
  }
  .legal-page p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .legal-page a {
    color: #FB5607;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .legal-page {
      padding: 110px 20px 64px;
    }
  }
</style>
